// NAME & INTRO 
"Val.Name": "Val",
"Val.Introduction": "Hey, Farmer. Be careful, there's an abundance of Rock Crabs in East Scarp - tainted and otherwise. A crabundance, if you will.$23#$b#I shouldn't quit my day job as a dungeon delver, my jokes are in ruins.$23",
// COMMUNITY CENTER BUNDLES  
"Val.JojaBegin": "It doesn't surprise me that Joja was able to buy out the Community Center. That's capitalism at work, I suppose.$24",
"Val.CCBegin": "Have you started revitalizing the Community Center, @? That's a noble effort. Good luck!$1",
"Val.CCBus": "Nice job, @! The bus will make it much easier to go to the desert. I haven't been to the Skull Cavern in a while, I should sharpen my swords.$31",
"Val.CCMinecart": "So you're saying you can hop in a mine cart and navigate all over The Valley with it? That sounds safe.$29",
"Val.CCComplete": "Congratulations on all your hard work, @. It's so nice to see the Community Center up and running again, it's been ages since anyone acknowledged it.$26",
"Val.MovieTheater": "Wanna go see a flick, @? It's my treat, since you're the one who went through all the trouble to rebuild from those ruins.$1#$b#Nothing does your arteries as good as an evening full of Flavacol popcorn!$20",
// BIRTHDAYS
"Val.BirthdayReminder.Hector": "I was stumped on what to get Hector for his birthday until I noticed him just laying face-first in the dirt the other day. Bar of soap it is.$27",
"Val.BirthdayReminder.Coriander": "So, question. Do we sing Coriander the 'happy birthday' song? I don't know about you, but I'd get stage fright singing in front of an award winning vocalist.$22",
"Val.BirthdayReminder.Roslin": "Roslin's birthday is coming up. I'm proud to say I'm wise enough to know not to ask her age. I love not getting fireballs thrown at my face. $1",
"Val.BirthdayReminder.Dandelion": "Dandelion's birthday is just around the corner, and my brilliant plan is to challenge her to a contest of strength. I know I'll lose, because that woman's a brick house, but it's the thought that counts.$0",
"Val.BirthdayReminder.Arden": "I thought getting Arden a gift would be difficult, being a dragon and all. Turns out, her interest in alcohol is extremely stereotypical, so I just let her raid my liquor cabinet.$25",
// END OF SEASON
"Val.SpringEnd": "Wow, Spring's over and done with already... Did you have a productive open to the year? Guess you'll be busy preparing the fields for Summer, huh?$20",
"Val.SummerEnd": "Suppose your summer crops are about ready to die off, @? That's alright. Just means it's time for a change; hardly a bad thing.$17",
"Val.FallEnd": "Winter's coming... Can't say I'm looking forward to it, but Spring will come back to us eventually.$27",
"Val.WinterEnd": "Thank goodness. The sun will shine on us again soon enough. Looking forward to the change of season.$25",
// SVE COMMUNITY DAY
"Val.CommunityCenter.01": "I'm so glad the everyone makes the effort to spend time together here. Stuff like this makes The Valley feel like home.$26",
"Val.CommunityCenter.02": "Good to see you here, @. Just doing the rounds and catching up with everyone. Sometimes it's hard to make time to see your friends, so I'm glad the townsfolk are committed to gathering together like this once a season.$20",
"Val.CommunityCenter.03": "Honestly, it's nice to be able to catch up with Marlon. Me and the old man don't get to hang out much outside of work. This is like, the only time I don't get a lecture on safe dungeon delving.$23",
// FESTIVALS (DAY BEFORE)
"Val.EggFestival": "The egg festival is tomorrow! The first big event to ring in the new year, huh? Hope your egg-hunting skills are sharp, @, I hear you've got some pretty tough competition.$17",
"Val.FlowerDance": "I love dancing, actually. I was big into the club scene back in college, but... Well, that's a very different sort of dancing, usually with a lot more liquor.$27",
"Val.Luau": "Tradition is important, of course, but doesn't it just seem really short sighted to blindly throw a ton of different things into one soup? I love taking risks, but that seems a little much.$27",
"Val.MoonlightJelly": "Tomorrow's celebration is my second favorite, next to Spirit's Eve. I can see the Jellies from the cove from right outside my house. It's breathtaking.$4",
"Val.SDVFair": "The fair is tomorrow, @! Are you going to bring pumpkins?$31#$b#I'm just saying, if I was voting and it was all pumpkins, you'd win.$23",
"Val.SpiritsEve": "So, there are a few rules to be followed on Spirit's Eve, back from when I was a kid.$17#$b#One, always check your candy. Two, always wear a costume. Three, always have treats on hand to give out.$23#$b#Finally, never blow out a Jack o' Lantern before midnight. That's the most important one.$31",
"Val.IceFestival": "Festival of Ice tomorrow, huh? I'm not one for fishing, by any means. But I can throw a mean snowball - and, hey, if you can dodge an Iridium Bat...$22",
"Val.NightMarket": "Oh, that's right. The Night Market's going on! I'd forgotten.$1#$b#Maybe I'll stop by and see if they've got anything from Gotoro for sale. Someone's bound to have smuggled in something interesting.$20",
"Val.WinterStar": "I don't like Winter, but I love giving gifts. If I can't pull off a grand gesture, I try to be as specific to the recipient as I can.$4",
// ROMANTIC (NEGATIVE)
"Val.Breakup": "Oh, s- @, I'm sorry you feel that way. And I'm sorry if I've done something to lead you to this decision.$24#$b#Hopefully, with enough time, we can be friends again. But I understand if you'd like space for a while.$25",
"Val.Divorced ": "Hey, @. Considering our prior relationship, I'd like some space. Unless it's an emergency, I'd appreciate it if you left me alone.$7",  
"Val.SpouseFarmhouseClutter": "Hey, it's pretty cluttered in here. Would you mind tidying up some of your stuff?$24",
"Val.SpouseMonstersInHouse": "Stand back, @! There's creatures afoot!$3",
"Val.WipedMemory": "Hey, uh!... Huh, sorry. For a second, I thought I knew you. Hm. I had a joke to make, but...$7#$b#It's in... ruins? That doesn't make any sense. Uh, anyway...$6", 
// ROMANTIC (POSITIVE)
"Val.SpouseGiftJealous": "It was so thoughtful of you to give {0} a {1}! This is why I love you, @.$4", 
"Val.Stardrop": "I found this growing in the Quarry Mine, believe it or not. I hope it tastes as good as you do.$4",
// RESORT
"Val.Resort.01": "Just taking a little break from running around, @. Be sure to put on some sunscreen if you're going to spend a lot of time out and about.$17",
"Val.Resort.02": "I could probably fall asleep here, but I sleep like a rock and I'd probably miss the boat back...$27",
"Val.Resort.03": "One nice thing about the beach is getting to show off all the scars. I got a lot of them from adventuring, but I'll admit I'm most proud of the ones on my chest.$10",
// GREEN RAIN
"Val.GreenRain": "I've never seen rain like this before, even with all the time I spent in Pelican Town as a kid. I hope it's a good omen.$22",
"Val.GreenRainFinished": "The rain was pretty intense, but it didn't seem to have any negative side effects. Everything is so lush right now, I'm sure Hector's excited.$26",
"Val.GreenRain2": "Now that I've gotten to know Hector a bit more, I'm pretty convinced this is his doing.$27",
// POLYAMORY 
"Val.MarriedMonogamousNPC": "Sorry, @! I'm flattered, but you're with a monogamous partner, so I'd be intruding on the rules of your relationship...$29",
// TRASH REACT 
"Val.DumpsterDiveComment": "If you wanted to dig for treasure, you could try... uh, the Mines, and not the trash?$27",
// SLINGSHOT 
"Val.HitBySlingshot": "Ow! Watch your aim, stay in the range if you're an amateur!$21",
// LOCATION ENTRIES 
"Val.VillageInn": "Rosa, you make a damn fine cup of coffee./It's so homey in here./Why are the floors covered in hay?", 
"Val.ArtificerHouse": "Home sweet home...!/Time to get back to working on my campaign./My dogs are barking...",
"Val.EastScarp": "Oh, there's the smell of sea air./Was that a Rock Crab?/This town has so many good sitting spots...",
// LOW HEART
"Val.LowHeart.01": "You pick up skills really quickly, @. It's super impressive, and I commend you for your dedication to learning so many different things.$0",
"Val.LowHeart.02": "Wilderness Golems are especially ornery when they're on the surface, most of all when the weather is nice.$29#$b#At least they're easier to manage than Stone Golems. Keep an eye out for them, they hit pretty hard.$27",
"Val.LowHeart.03": "Are you a sword, hammer, or dagger sort of person? Be sure to maintenance your weapon, especially if the weather is poor or if you're heavy handed with it.$26",
"Val.LowHeart.04": "Crabs keep breaking into my house. Stygium crabs, sure. But also Rock Crabs. And regular crabs.$15",
"Val.LowHeart.05": "Keep your chin up, @. Even if today is a bit on the rough side, tomorrow always has a chance of being better.",
"Val.LowHeart.06": "Seen anything fun on your adventures, @? Big ol' monsters? Weird plants? Sordid affairs between townsfolk? I'd love to listen over a drink of your choice.$10",
"Val.LowHeart.07": "The desert trader has these artifact troves; they've got things like Dwarven Gadgets and other relics inside. Problem is, I'm not sure how it's all sourced.$11",
"Val.LowHeart.08": "I picked a scab from an injury I got fighting monsters, which... just made it worse. I do this every time, without fail. Don't pick your wounds, @.$29",
"Val.LowHeart.09": "I love watching the sun rise. Waking up early is something of a bummer, but the shimmering gleam of sunlight on the surface of the ocean is worth it.$4",
"Val.LowHeart.10": "Did you know Frost Bats have trouble surviving in humid temperatures? You're not likely to see them on the surface. Fruit Bats, though? We've got several colonies of those.$26",
"Val.LowHeart.11": "What's under a Metal Head helmet, anyway? I've always wondered, but I've never gone out of my way to go try and pry one apart. Some mysteries are better left unsolved.$27",
"Val.LowHeart.12": "When I first started delving as a kid, I was particularly fascinated by the Dust Sprites. Cute little things, aren't they?$9#$b#Wish they weren't such a good way to gather coal, though.$2",
"Val.LowHeart.13": "I wonder if Marnie needs any help around the ranch. I'll happily trade time spent doing manual labor to be able to pet the critters.$4",
"Val.LowHeart.14": "Hiking in the Deep Mountains is fantastic. There's so much to see, there's weird goats to pet - I'm not sure I could ask for more, honestly. And! There's the north shore, which has a brilliant view.$26",
"Val.LowHeart.15": "There must be something up with the lightbulb on the pier on the main Scarp beach. I swear, it's green sometimes...$29",
"Val.LowHeart.16": "I've seen and heard of a lot of strange supernatural phenomenons up on the surface, cryptids and the like. Really, I think it's just monsters with varying abilities and levels of intelligence.$22",
"Val.LowHeart.17": "Have you ever seen a Squid Kid? I'm not sure why they're even called that. They don't look like squids but they DO shoot fireballs. Take care if you run into one, @. $29",
"Val.LowHeart.18": "I think the Golden Masks you can occasionally find in the Skull Cave are ceremonial versions of the ones worn by Shadow Shamans.$22#$b#I haven't met a Shadow Folk from Calico Desert, but I don't doubt they exist.$23",
"Val.LowHeart.19": "Every day, give yourself a present. It could be a nice new shirt, or a little nap, or half a pot of fresh coffee all to yourself! Don't ignore your own happiness for the sake of others, @.$25",
"Val.LowHeart.20": "Have you ever read 'The Great Gatsbish? It's my favorite book of all time. It's relatively short and the prose is lovely, if you'd ever like to borrow my copy.$20#$b#It's about wanting to change the past. About obsession. About the masks we all wear, and how they're capable of cracking no matter how gilded they are.$25",
"Val.LowHeart.21": "I love parties. I love dancing, strong drinks, loud music. I'll go to ZuZu city to surround myself with strangers. After all, The larger the crowd, the more intimate it is.$17",
"Val.LowHeart.22": "I have a certain fondness for trinkets. Things from movies and books, mostly. I don't mind wearing my interests on my sleeve; it's vulnerable, and helps start conversations.$1",
"Val.LowHeart.23": "Do you like horror movies, @? We should watch one sometime. I love the classic slashers, but my favorite is about a Trick or Treater who enforces the rules of Spirit's Eve...$23",
"Val.LowHeart.24": "What kind of music are you into, @? I'm on the glam metal end of the spectrum, but my favorite band is more in the vein of ...'spooky pop-rock'.$9#$b#I have a lot of records stored under my bed, but I bet you a third of them are collector variants of the same few albums.$1",
"Val.LowHeart.25": "I need to clean the stylus on my record player. Haven't dusted the turntable in a bit, either. I'd best get on that!$1#$b#I keep the records I don't listen to often stored away. But sometimes, I get the urge to pull out a classic...$17",
"Val.LowHeart.26": "I got this little bear figurine from a tchotchke shop across the street from a diner I went to... what was it called, Twede's? They had really good cherry pie.$22#$b#Anyway, I'm pretty sure it's haunted. It's got a certain look in it's eye. But I won't throw it away because I feel like that's somehow worse.$27",
"Val.LowHeart.27": "I have an insatiable lust for crab cakes. I know what I must do... and East Scarp will provide.$32",
"Val.LowHeart.28": "When I read stories, I tend to appreciate narratives that read more like character studies. It's fun to really delve into someone's psyche to understand their perspective.$0#$b#You can take it a step further and understand the context behind why a story was written. Sometimes things like time period matter, and I just think that's neat.$1",
"Val.LowHeart.29": "I was re-reading one of my favorite tabletop setting supplements recently, Curse of Vlahd. It's a horror-tragedy about a party of adventurers being tormented by a vampire...$26",
"Val.LowHeart.30": "One of the games that I have, that I never run, is Vampire the Facade. If I'm going to do something with creatures of the night, it would be Curse of Vlahd.$29",
"Val.LowHeart.31": "Sometimes, I like to make casts of dice sets and make custom ones out of resin. It's really fun, and you can do a lot of interesting colors. I'll try metal ones next!$1",
"Val.LowHeart.32": "Hope you're able to get some recreational reading in, @. It's good for the brain, good for the heart. You can borrow off my shelves, if you'd like.$25",
"Val.LowHeart.33": "I've been marathoning my favorite movies lately. The Pharaoh, Colorado Jones, Treasure Universe... What are yours, @?$26",
"Val.LowHeart.34": "My horns? They're made of keratin, like nails are. Painting them actually protects them. Sometimes I go with orange, sometimes I go with clear coat.$17",
"Val.LowHeart.35": "I have a tail, but I keep it tucked into my pants. If I'm not tripping on it, someone's stepping on it. If someone's not stepping on it, a monster's trying to bite it...$27",
"Val.LowHeart.36": "I tore my pillow in my sleep on accident. Horn got caught on it...$11#$b#Aw, well. Good excuse as any to get a newer, fluffier one.$10",
"Val.LowHeart.37": "I've traveled a lot, but the seasons here are a lot more drastic than what I've seen elsewhere. I like that, though. It's part of The Valley's character.$1",
"Val.LowHeart.38": "A skeleton nicked me real good in the shoulder the other day. Do they use the bones of their fallen brethren to throw at their opponents? Hilarious, but morbid.$27",
"Val.LowHeart.39": "Do you go to the hot springs in the mountains often? I've been up that way a few times, mostly at night. It's good for the muscles. You exert yourself a lot, be sure to give yourself grace.$25",
"Val.LowHeart.40": "I'm trying to cut down on my caffeine consumption. So when I get up, I only have one cup of coffee. And then I have another with breakfast...$0#$e#And usually I've got one in a to-go cup on the way to the Deep Dark. And then that's it for the day...$6#$e#Oh, besides the one I have with lunch, you've got to have one with lunch. And then an espresso around two, you know, to chase off the inevitable migraine... and THEN that's it...$15#$e#Except for the one I have when I get home, and the one right before bed... So, yeah! Really been cutting back. Very proud of myself.$17",
"Val.LowHeart.41": "Making chainmail is a time consuming process. I forged rings and wove them together with pliers. Now, all I have to do is repair the shirt once in a while.$20",
"Val.LowHeart.42": "Technically, farriers specialize in metalworking associated with hooves, not blacksmiths. I learned to do both because I love horseshoes.$25",
"Val.LowHeart.43": "When swinging a blacksmith hammer, you do want to lift it above your head and then swing. More force is better to move the steel in a short time before the blade cools.$1",
"Val.LowHeart.44": "I'm pretty sure smithing and adventuring keep me in shape, but smithing is less about being able to lift a heavy hammer and more about being able to slam a light one down a thousand times.$28",
"Val.LowHeart.45": "I love working with leather, but my favorite part of the process is tooling. I can space out and lose myself in detailing. Mostly, I enjoy floral designs!$1",
"Val.LowHeart.46": "Things I've made from leather? My armor, smithing apron, belts, gloves, holsters. And... plenty of other stuff. Leather is terribly versatile. $28",
"Val.LowHeart.47": "If you asked me to pick between Cherry Pie and Pumpkin Pie, I wouldn't be able to. Great pie and warm coffee really invoke a sense of nostalgia for me.$4",
"Val.LowHeart.48": "I stopped in at Rosa's and she had freshly made Maple Bars. Like any logical person, I bought three and ate two right there with a cup of coffee. The last one's for after dinner.$1",
"Val.LowHeart.49": "How do I take my coffee? Black as midnight on a moonless night. But sometimes, I add a drop of Salish Bourbon as a little present for the day.$17",
"Val.LowHeart.50": "I've considered moving back to the Fern Islands, where I went to school. But outside The Valley, there's a vast carelessness that I don't think I can adapt to.$2",
// HIGH HEART
"Val.HighHeart.01": "My childhood taletop character's name was Gideon Weaveforger. Clearly he stuck with me, since I ended up going to school for metallurgical engineering. It was probably really healthy to have an outlet for a fledgling interest.#$b#I miss him, in a way. Because now I run games eternally instead of playing them... Maybe I can sneak him in as a cameo.",
"Val.HighHeart.02": "I'm an Artificer, but I hold the title 'Doctor'. I mean, I AM a Doctor, just not THAT kind of Doctor. I have a doctorate.#$b#It's not the same thing. You can't help people with a doctorate. You just sit there and you're useless!",
"Val.HighHeart.03": "Back when I was in college, I was the president of the boardgaming club. We managed to repeatedly secure funding to buy games and supplements and then test them out. Not sure that's how the finances should've worked...#$b#But, we had a great time, and we even funded a few trips to local conventions and tried to volunteer for them when we could.",
"Val.HighHeart.04": "You should come over for cocktails sometime, @. Or mocktials, if that's your preference. I enjoy making drinks, it's a way for me to express my hospitality.#$b#Most of the time, I want my drinks neat. But I'm also big on things that are citrus forward; I've a soft spot for kettle sours... ",
"Val.HighHeart.05": "Did you know that skeletons can do magic? I didn't either, until one of them froze my feet to the floor. He even had a cape on. It billowed dramatically behind him as he charged at me.#$b#Goes to show it's always worth approaching the mines with caution. Stay safe, @. ",
"Val.HighHeart.06": "We don't know much about how Mummies animate, since the only way to incapacitate them is with bombs and that doesn't leave much to study.#$b#Capturing a live Mummy seems needlessly cruel, so unfortunately the best we can do is study the strange tombs they tend to wander after they've been dealt with. I'd love to take it a step further than that, but I don't want to get cursed.",
"Val.HighHeart.07": "Have you ever seen those Dwarvish Sentries inside the volcano on Ginger Island? For all that they're slow, they come at you with reckless abandon. Clearly, the Dwarves had something they want to protect somewhere in there.#$b#It's worth exploring, but be careful navigating that place, @, I wouldn't want to hear secondhand about anything happening to you.",
"Val.HighHeart.08": "I suspect there are variants of Pepper Rexes we haven't seen yet. For example, a lot of the bones we find in prehistoric spaces don't match the living specimens, but they're dated within the last twenty years.#$b#There are Stygium Rexes in the Deep Dark, but I expect there's more, since those are normal Pepper Rexes, just corrupted...",
"Val.HighHeart.09": "Do you know what the bottom half of a Duggy looks like? It's been on my mind all day. For all we know, they can be serpentine, and nobody's bothered to pull one up out of the hole and check.#$b#While I respect that the academic community hasn't deemed this important, I respectfully disagree with their decision. That being said, we should go uproot some Duggies.",
"Val.HighHeart.10": "I'm not sold on it yet, but there's a substantial amount of anthropological evidence supporting the hypothesis that Goblins and Dwarves are related. It's just a theory, though!#$b#I think it's interesting but a lot of it's circumstantial. Personally, lean into the idea that they cohabited before the Elemental Wars rather than stem from the same exact ancestor.",
"Val.HighHeart.11": "I really want to know how a Treasure Chest can wind up in a Ghost Fish pond. Ponds are man-made, so where are they getting them from? They can't go treasure hunting, fish don't even have thumbs. Or am I just overthinking?$27",
"Val.HighHeart.12": "I've always wanted a big library in my house, kind of like in the movies. I mean, it's a mix of textbooks, fiction and tabletop supplements, but books are books. It doesn't matter what you read as long as you enjoy it.#$b#You're more than welcome to borrow something, @. And, unlike Gunther, I don't hold grudges over late fees...",
"Val.HighHeart.13": "There are difficult to decipher messages on the walls of the Skull Cavern. Have you ever noticed them, @? Something about heroes. Maybe we can go together and have a look; I'm sure there's something interesting to be discovered there.#$b#There are also really strange skeletons in the desert that I'd love to take a closer look at. Draconic remains are far and few in between...",
"Val.HighHeart.14": "So I climbed through the hatch on the roof of The Guild and watched the sunset last night. Beer in hand, just listening to the waves. It was amazing. There's something really special about The Valley, @.#$b#You should join me sometime. It's a really special view, and I'm more than happy to share it.",
"Val.HighHeart.15": "I got bitten up by one of those flying Serpents in the Skull Cave. Those things are fierce, aren't they? I'd rather deal with an entire horde of skeletons. They're slower, and they don't swarm.#$b#Some skeletons can do magic, which is frustrating, but Serpents are so vicious in their persuit I don't think they're comparable.",
"Val.HighHeart.16": "20 some-odd years adventuring will leave you with a lot of scars. I was self-conscious of them at first, but now they're a point of pride - Even the new ones.#$b#I feel like that particular injury was actually a turning point; I feel like I was set on a different path after you patched me up.",
"Val.HighHeart.17": "Sometimes I find old arms deep in the mines. Swords, hammers and the like. I can't help but wonder if the ghosts that haunt those spaces are just trying to warn newer adventurers, like they don't want them to share the same fate.#$b#I've never been one for looting - things that are of value belong in a museum, and ore veins are for everyone. So I tend to just leave old equipment where it is.",
"Val.HighHeart.18": "My depth perception isn't great on the right side. It does make delving a little harder, as if I didn't have to be careful before...#$b#Sometimes I feel very sensitive to the light, but that's nothing an eyepatch can't address.",
"Val.HighHeart.19": "I've had fire-eyes as long as I can remember; I assume it's something to do with being a Troll. I've been a bit disappointed at how I've lost color in one, but most everyone has reassured me that it scarred over well.",
"Val.HighHeart.20": "",
