// SEASONAL
"Val.Spring.1": "It's getting warmer out. You can tell by the Spring in folks' step.$31",
"Val.Spring.2": "What did the florist say during springtime, @?... Business is blooming.$32",
"Val.Spring.3": "I've got a Spring in my step, @, how about you?$23 ",
"Val.Spring.4": "Now that the cold is gone, I'm feeling... like a tree. You know, very re-leafed.$17",
"Val.Spring.5": "How does the sun listen to music, @? Well... on the ray-dio, of course.$1",
"Val.Summer.1": "Howdy, @. Will I sea you on the beach this Summer?$31",
"Val.Summer.2": "Pardon my resting beach face, @. But now that you're here, anything is... popsicle.$32 [233]",
"Val.Summer.3": "Water you waiting for, @? Let's get everyone together and go swimming. The weather's just right!$23",
"Val.Summer.4": "I was reading a novel about a man trapped at sea, and you can say it made me very... em-ocean-al.$17",
"Val.Summer.5": "My favorite genre of book? Oh, it's fantasy, but in the Summer it's fanta-sea.$1",
"Val.Fall.1": "I could go for some mulled cider right now, or some roasted corn, or apple pie with some ice cream...$17",
"Val.Fall.2": "It's sunflower season, right? Do you cook the seeds? Oh, you could do that with pumpkins, too. It's delicious!$1",
"Val.Fall.3": "Are you an apple cider person, a pumpkin spice person, or a hot chocolate person? 'Tis the season for all the best warm drinks.$26",
"Val.Fall.4": "Don't blow a Jack o' Lantern out before midnight, @, Or you'll invite creatures of the night into your home. Good for you if you're doing it intentionally, though.$28",
"Val.Fall.5": "Life starts over again when it gets crisp in the Fall.$25",
"Val.Winter.1": "I have a really hard time in Winter. Spending time in the Deep Dark this time of year just makes it worse because of the lack of sunlight. It's... uh, snow joke.$24",
"Val.Winter.2": "Sorry if I give you the cold shoulder, @. I tend to be moody this time of year, and ...ice people out.$15",
"Val.Winter.3": "Guess you can say this dreary weather has me feeling really frost-rated. I really hate this yearly... Winter-uption.$11",
"Val.Winter.4": "Hey, @. Aren't you a sight for sore-ice? How are you holding up this season? Maintaining the farm this time of year must be easier sled than done.$27",
"Val.Winter.5": "Winter's challenging to get through, but I suppose everything has it's... highs and froze.$22",
// GIFTS GIVEN
"Val.Gift.1": "Hey @! I found this down below, and thought you might be interested.$1 [96 97 98 99 100 101 103 104 105 106 108 109 110 111 112 113 115 116 117 118 119 120 121 122 123]",
"Val.Gift.2": "Hey, @! I met with the desert trader - I had some unusual minerals they were looking for, so we did a little exchange. This is an excellent study piece! [124 125]$1",
"Val.Gift.3": "Hey, @. I dug up a fossil, check it out!$1[586 587 588 589]",
"Val.Gift.4": "Hey, @! I've got a bone to pick with- nah, just kidding. Just found something down below you might need for the museum.$17 [579 580 581 582 583 584 585]",
"Val.Gift.5": "Hey, @! I found something weird on Ginger Island. I think it might be of use to you.$26[820 821 822 823 824 825 826 827 828]",
"Val.Gift.6": "Hey, @! I had some extra ore and hammered out some ingots. Figured I'd share.$1 #$action AddItem {{Random: (O)Copper_Bar, (O)Iron_Bar, (O)Gold_Bar, (O)Iridium_Bar}} {{Random: {{Range: 1,3}}}}",
"Val.Gift.7": "Hey, @! I collected an over-abundance of coal, and I figured I'd share the wealth. #$action AddItem (O)Coal {{Random: {{Range: 20,50}}}}",
"Val.Gift.8": "Hey, @! Got this when I cracked a geode, figured you might want it for the museum.$1 [538 539 540 541 542 543 544 545 546 547 548 549 550 551 552 553 554 555 556 557 558 559 560 561 562 563 564 565 566 567 568 569 570 571 572 573 574 575 576 577 578",
"Val.Gift.9": "Are you being safe in your dungeon delving, @? Here's something that'll help...$25 [349 351]",
"Val.Gift.10": "Hey, @! Guess what? I got you a treat, just in case you haven't gotten one for yourself today.$17 #$action AddItem (O)DN.SnS_ChocolateOrange",
